/* =====================================================================
   PRIMARY HYPEROXALURIA (PH1 / PH2 / PH3) — QSP Mechanistic Map
   including secondary (enteric) hyperoxaluria as the SAME equations
   evaluated with a different source term
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE ORGANISING IDEA

     OXALATE IS A TERMINAL METABOLITE. HUMANS HAVE NO OXALATE-DEGRADING
     ENZYME. THEREFORE PRIMARY HYPEROXALURIA IS NOT A DISEASE WITH A
     SEVERITY SCORE — IT IS AN UNCLOSED MASS BALANCE, AND EVERY CLINICAL
     FEATURE IS THE ARITHMETIC OF WHERE THE UNEXCRETED OXALATE WENT.

         hepatic production  =  renal excretion
                             +  enteric elimination
                             +  d(tissue burden)/dt

     There is deliberately NO node on this map called "disease severity"
     and no parameter in the companion mrgsolve model that sets it. The
     phenotype is the residual of the three-way balance above.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   WHY THAT ONE EQUATION EXPLAINS THE WHOLE DISEASE

   Rearranged, the balance says the tissue burden grows whenever
   production exceeds what the kidney and gut can remove. The gut term
   is small and roughly fixed. So the entire natural history is governed
   by ONE ratio:

            production (set by genotype)
            ----------------------------
            renal clearance (set by GFR)

   and the two arms of that ratio move in OPPOSITE directions over a
   lifetime, because the oxalate the kidney excretes is what destroys
   the kidney. The denominator is eaten by the numerator. That is the
   whole disease, and it produces three consequences that no additive
   severity model can generate:

     (1) A THRESHOLD, NOT A SLOPE. While GFR is preserved the kidney
         clears essentially all of the production, so PLASMA oxalate is
         near normal and the disease is a stone disease. Once GFR falls
         far enough that clearance drops below production, the residual
         has nowhere to go but tissue; plasma oxalate rises as ~1/GFR
         and crosses the calcium-oxalate solubility limit of plasma
         (~30 umol/L). Below that GFR the disease changes organ system —
         it stops being nephrology and becomes bone, retina, heart,
         nerve and skin. Systemic oxalosis is not a late complication;
         it is the same equation past a root.

     (2) A RUNAWAY. Crystals deposited in the kidney destroy nephrons,
         which lowers GFR, which raises plasma oxalate, which deposits
         more crystals (cluster 12). The feedback is positive and its
         loop gain rises as GFR falls, which is why the terminal decline
         in PH1 is abrupt rather than linear.

     (3) A BIOMARKER THAT INVERTS. Urinary oxalate is (renal clearance)
         x (plasma oxalate). Early on, clearance is fixed and Uox tracks
         production — it is a valid efficacy biomarker. Late on, falling
         GFR pulls Uox DOWN while the disease accelerates. There is a
         GFR at which dUox/dt changes sign with production unchanged.
         See cluster 21: this is why one drug needed two different
         registration endpoints in two different trials.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE ENZYMOLOGY, AND WHY THE DRUG TARGET IS NOT THE BROKEN GENE

   Glyoxylate is the pivot metabolite. It sits in the hepatocyte with
   two possible fates:

       DETOXIFY   glyoxylate + L-alanine --AGT/PLP--> glycine + pyruvate
                  (peroxisomal, AGXT gene, needs pyridoxal-5'-phosphate)

       POISON     glyoxylate --LDHA--> OXALATE
                  (cytosolic, irreversible, terminal)

   PH1 is loss of the detoxifying branch (AGXT). The flux does not stop;
   it is re-routed. So the rational drug targets are NOT AGT — you
   cannot easily restore a missing enzyme — but the two flanking
   reactions:

       UPSTREAM   block glycolate -> glyoxylate   (HAO1 / glycolate
                  oxidase; lumasiran). Glyoxylate is never made, so
                  GLYCOLATE accumulates instead. Glycolate is a benign,
                  freely filtered dead end. The rising plasma glycolate
                  is therefore not a side effect — it is the receipt.

       DOWNSTREAM block glyoxylate -> oxalate     (LDHA; nedosiran,
                  stiripentol). Oxalate is never made, so GLYOXYLATE
                  accumulates instead — a reactive aldehyde, which is
                  why this branch carries a theoretical liability the
                  upstream branch does not.

   Both are SUBSTRATE REDUCTION THERAPY: they treat a toxic-accumulation
   disease by turning down the tap rather than repairing the drain.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE RESULT THIS MAP EXISTS TO GENERATE: DELIVERY, NOT TARGET,
   DECIDES WHICH DISEASE THE DRUG TREATS

   LDHA is the last step for PH1, PH2 AND PH3 — all three funnel through
   it. A naive reading says an LDHA siRNA should treat all three. It
   does not: nedosiran works in PH1 and failed in PH2.

   The reason is drawn on this map as a geometric fact rather than a
   footnote. A GalNAc-conjugated siRNA is taken up by the
   asialoglycoprotein receptor, which is expressed at ~500,000 copies
   per HEPATOCYTE and essentially nowhere else (cluster 14). So the
   knockdown is hepatocyte-restricted by construction. That is fine when
   the oxalate is made in hepatocytes:

       AGXT   — liver-specific expression      -> PH1 oxalate is hepatic
       GRHPR  — expressed in liver AND kidney  -> PH2 oxalate is partly
                and other tissues                 EXTRAHEPATIC
       HOGA1  — liver (+ kidney) mitochondrial -> PH3 intermediate

   A liver-restricted drug cannot silence an enzyme deficiency whose
   consequence is generated outside the liver. Nodes OX_SRC_HEP and
   OX_SRC_EXTRAHEP exist for exactly this reason, and in the companion
   model the PH2 non-response is produced by moving mass between those
   two nodes — no separate "PH2 resistance" parameter is used. A
   small-molecule LDH inhibitor that distributes to kidney as well as
   liver (stiripentol) is drawn on a DIFFERENT arrow into the same
   target for the same reason.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   THE THREE THERAPEUTIC LAYERS, WHICH ARE NOT INTERCHANGEABLE

     LAYER A  PRODUCTION   changes the mass balance
              lumasiran, nedosiran, stiripentol, pyridoxine (genotype-
              gated), liver replacement, gene therapy
     LAYER B  CRYSTALLISATION  changes NOTHING in the mass balance and
              still prevents stones — hyperhydration, potassium citrate,
              magnesium, neutral phosphate. Uox in mmol/day is untouched;
              only the CONCENTRATION and the inhibitor activity change,
              so relative supersaturation falls. This is the clearest
              demonstration on the map that the stone endpoint is driven
              by a ratio, not by a flux.
     LAYER C  REMOVAL      dialysis, enteric degradation (Oxalobacter)
              — and cluster 19 shows by arithmetic that conventional
              thrice-weekly haemodialysis CANNOT match PH1 production.

   Layer B protects the kidney but never prevents systemic oxalosis.
   Layer C is quantitatively insufficient alone. Only Layer A closes the
   balance. That ordering is the map's therapeutic argument.

   ---------------------------------------------------------------------
   STRUCTURE (21 clusters, 250+ nodes)

     1  Genetics and genotype-phenotype
     2  Substrate supply into the glyoxylate pool
     3  Hepatocyte peroxisome — the AGT reaction
     4  Hepatocyte cytosol — LDHA and the terminal step
     5  Hepatocyte mitochondrion — HOGA1 / hydroxyproline route
     6  Oxalate systemic distribution and the solubility limit
     7  Bone — the reservoir that both buffers and betrays
     8  Soft-tissue oxalosis
     9  Renal oxalate handling
    10  Crystallisation physical chemistry (Layer B target)
    11  Crystal-induced tubulointerstitial injury
    12  The nephron-loss positive feedback loop
    13  Gut-kidney oxalate axis (and enteric hyperoxaluria)
    14  siRNA PK/PD — GalNAc/ASGPR/RISC
    15  Pyridoxine and chaperone rescue
    16  Small molecules, gene therapy, experimental
    17  Supportive / crystallisation-directed therapy
    18  Dialysis kinetics
    19  Transplantation
    20  Clinical endpoints
    21  The measurement layer (biomarker inversion, assay traps)

   Arrow convention:  solid black = mass flux / conversion
                      solid blue  = activation / promotion
                      dashed red  = inhibition / blockade
                      dashed grey = modulation, measurement, annotation
   ===================================================================== */

digraph PH1_QSP {
  graph [rankdir=LR, splines=spline, overlap=false, nodesep=0.30, ranksep=0.55,
         fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=11, compound=true,
         labelloc="t", label=<<B>PRIMARY HYPEROXALURIA — QSP MECHANISTIC MAP</B><BR/>
<FONT POINT-SIZE="12">Oxalate is a terminal metabolite: production = renal excretion + enteric elimination + d(tissue burden)/dt</FONT><BR/>
<FONT POINT-SIZE="10">PH1 (AGXT) · PH2 (GRHPR) · PH3 (HOGA1) · enteric hyperoxaluria as the same balance with a different source term</FONT>>,
         bgcolor="white"];
  node  [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10, style="filled,rounded",
         shape=box, penwidth=1.1];
  edge  [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=8, arrowsize=0.65, penwidth=1.0];

  /* ---------- colour language -------------------------------------- */
  /* gene/genotype        #ede7f6 purple  */
  /* metabolite pool      #fff8e1 amber   */
  /* enzyme               #e8f5e9 green   */
  /* organ/structure      #e3f2fd blue    */
  /* injury/inflammation  #ffebee red     */
  /* drug                 #fce4ec pink    */
  /* biomarker            #e0f7fa cyan    */
  /* endpoint             #f3e5f5 violet  */
  /* arithmetic/identity  #eceff1 grey    */

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 1 — GENETICS AND GENOTYPE-PHENOTYPE
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_gen {
    label=<<B>1. GENETICS — three genes, three diseases, one metabolite</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#f6f3fb"; color="#7e57c2"; fontsize=12;

    AGXT      [label="AGXT  (2q37.3)\nalanine:glyoxylate aminotransferase\nPEROXISOMAL, LIVER-SPECIFIC\n→ PH1 (~80% of PH)", fillcolor="#ede7f6"];
    GRHPR     [label="GRHPR  (9p13.2)\nglyoxylate/hydroxypyruvate reductase\nCYTOSOLIC, WIDELY EXPRESSED\n→ PH2 (~10%)", fillcolor="#ede7f6"];
    HOGA1     [label="HOGA1  (10q24.2)\n4-hydroxy-2-oxoglutarate aldolase\nMITOCHONDRIAL, liver + kidney\n→ PH3 (~10%)", fillcolor="#ede7f6"];
    SLC26A1   [label="SLC26A1 / SLC26A6\nsulfate/oxalate anion exchangers\ncandidate modifier of enteric\nsecretion and renal handling", fillcolor="#ede7f6"];

    ALL_G170R [label="p.Gly170Arg  (G170R)\ncommonest PH1 allele (~30% of alleles)\nprotein FOLDS but is MISTARGETED\nto mitochondrion → PYRIDOXINE-RESPONSIVE", fillcolor="#d1c4e9"];
    ALL_F152I [label="p.Phe152Ile  (F152I)\nfolding/dimerisation defect\nPYRIDOXINE-RESPONSIVE", fillcolor="#d1c4e9"];
    ALL_I244T [label="p.Ile244Thr\nfounder allele (N Africa, Canary Is.)\naggregation-prone; partial B6 response", fillcolor="#ede7f6"];
    ALL_G82E  [label="p.Gly82Glu\nPLP-binding-site destroyed\nNOT rescuable by pyridoxine", fillcolor="#ede7f6"];
    ALL_NULL  [label="nonsense / frameshift / large deletion\nno protein at all\nB6-UNRESPONSIVE, infantile phenotype", fillcolor="#b39ddb"];
    MINOR_HAP [label="minor allele haplotype (P11L)\ncis-acting; creates the mitochondrial\ntargeting sequence G170R needs\n→ required for the B6 phenotype", fillcolor="#ede7f6"];

    RESID_AGT [label="RESIDUAL AGT ACTIVITY  (0-100%)\nTHE SINGLE PARAMETER FROM WHICH\nTHE PHENOTYPE IS GENERATED", fillcolor="#eceff1", shape=box, penwidth=2.4, color="#37474f"];
    PHENO_INF [label="infantile oxalosis\nESKD in the first months of life\nresidual activity ≈ 0", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    PHENO_CHILD [label="childhood nephrolithiasis /\nnephrocalcinosis, ESKD in teens", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    PHENO_ADULT [label="adult recurrent stone former\nESKD in 4th-6th decade or never\nresidual activity 10-30%", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    PENETR   [label="incomplete penetrance / wide intrafamilial\nvariability — same genotype, different course\n(modifier + environment + diagnostic delay)", fillcolor="#eceff1"];

      ALL_G170R -> MINOR_HAP [dir=both, style=dashed, color="#78909c", label="cis"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 2 — SUBSTRATE SUPPLY INTO THE GLYOXYLATE POOL
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_sub {
    label=<<B>2. SUBSTRATE SUPPLY — where the glyoxylate comes from</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#fffdf5"; color="#f9a825"; fontsize=12;

    DIET_GLYCOLATE [label="dietary / microbial GLYCOLATE\n(leafy greens, fruit; minor)", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    DIET_HYPRO     [label="dietary + ENDOGENOUS\n4-HYDROXYPROLINE\ncollagen turnover, gelatin, meat\n→ ~20-45% of oxalate in PH", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    COLL_TURN      [label="collagen degradation flux\n(growth, immobilisation, bone resorption,\ncatabolic illness, corticosteroids)", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    DIET_GLYCINE   [label="glycine / serine", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    ASCORBATE      [label="ASCORBATE (vitamin C)\nnon-enzymatic degradation → oxalate\nhigh-dose supplements = added source", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    FRUCTOSE       [label="fructose / glycerol\n→ hydroxypyruvate / glyceraldehyde", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    EG_TOX         [label="ETHYLENE GLYCOL poisoning\nADH → glycolaldehyde → glycolate → glyoxylate\nTHE ACQUIRED PHENOCOPY of PH1\n(same node, different time constant)", fillcolor="#ffe0b2"];
    DIET_OXALATE   [label="DIETARY OXALATE\nspinach, rhubarb, nuts, tea, cocoa\n~100-200 mg/d ingested,\n~2-10% absorbed in health", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    GLYCOLALD      [label="glycolaldehyde", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];

    HYPRO_FLUX [label="hydroxyproline → glyoxylate flux\nWHY GROWTH AND IMMOBILISATION\nWORSEN PH", fillcolor="#eceff1"];

    COLL_TURN -> DIET_HYPRO [color=black];
    DIET_HYPRO -> HYPRO_FLUX [color=black];
    EG_TOX -> GLYCOLALD [color=black, label="ADH"];
    GLYCOLALD -> DIET_GLYCOLATE [color=black, label="ALDH"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 3 — HEPATOCYTE PEROXISOME (the AGT reaction)
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_perox {
    label=<<B>3. HEPATOCYTE PEROXISOME — glyoxylate detoxification (the branch PH1 loses)</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#f4fbf5"; color="#2e7d32"; fontsize=12;

    PEROX      [label="PEROXISOME\n(hepatocyte)", fillcolor="#e3f2fd", shape=box3d];
    GLYCOLATE_P [label="peroxisomal GLYCOLATE", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    GO_HAO1    [label="GLYCOLATE OXIDASE (GO)\nHAO1 gene, FMN-dependent\nglycolate + O2 → glyoxylate + H2O2\n★ LUMASIRAN TARGET", fillcolor="#c8e6c9", penwidth=2.0];
    H2O2       [label="H2O2 → catalase\n(peroxisomal oxidative load)", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    GLYOX_P    [label="PEROXISOMAL GLYOXYLATE\nthe pivot metabolite", fillcolor="#ffe082", penwidth=2.2];
    AGT_HOLO   [label="AGT holoenzyme (PLP-loaded dimer)\nglyoxylate + L-alanine → glycine + pyruvate\nTHE DETOXIFYING REACTION", fillcolor="#a5d6a7", penwidth=2.0];
    AGT_APO    [label="apo-AGT (no PLP)\ninactive; aggregation-prone;\nproteasome substrate", fillcolor="#e8f5e9"];
    AGT_MISTGT [label="MISTARGETED AGT (mitochondrial)\nenzymatically active but IN THE WRONG\nORGANELLE → no access to peroxisomal\nglyoxylate (the G170R lesion)", fillcolor="#e8f5e9"];
    PLP_LIV    [label="hepatic PYRIDOXAL-5'-PHOSPHATE (PLP)\ncofactor AND chemical chaperone", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    GLYCINE    [label="glycine + pyruvate\n(harmless products)", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    DAO        [label="D-amino acid oxidase (DAO)\nglycine → glyoxylate (minor)", fillcolor="#e8f5e9"];
    PEROX_LEAK [label="peroxisomal membrane permeability\nto glyoxylate\n(sets how much escapes to cytosol)", fillcolor="#eceff1"];
    HSP_CHAP   [label="HSP70 / HSP90 chaperone system\nfolding QC of nascent AGT", fillcolor="#e8f5e9"];
    PROTEASOME [label="ubiquitin-proteasome degradation\nof misfolded AGT", fillcolor="#e8f5e9"];

    GLYCOLATE_P -> GO_HAO1 [color=black];
    GO_HAO1 -> GLYOX_P [color=black, label="flux J_GO"];
    GO_HAO1 -> H2O2 [color=black, style=dashed];
    GLYOX_P -> AGT_HOLO [color=black];
    AGT_HOLO -> GLYCINE [color=black, label="J_AGT"];
    PLP_LIV -> AGT_HOLO [color="#1565c0", label="cofactor"];
    AGT_APO -> AGT_HOLO [color=black, label="+PLP"];
    PLP_LIV -> AGT_APO [style=dashed, color="#1565c0", label="chaperone\nrescue"];
    AGT_APO -> PROTEASOME [color=black];
    HSP_CHAP -> AGT_APO [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    DAO -> GLYOX_P [color=black];
    GLYOX_P -> PEROX_LEAK [color=black];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 4 — HEPATOCYTE CYTOSOL (LDHA, the terminal step)
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_cyto {
    label=<<B>4. HEPATOCYTE CYTOSOL — the irreversible step, and the salvage route PH2 loses</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#f4fbf5"; color="#2e7d32"; fontsize=12;

    GLYOX_C   [label="CYTOSOLIC GLYOXYLATE\nreactive 2-oxo aldehyde", fillcolor="#ffe082", penwidth=2.2];
    LDHA_LIV  [label="LDHA (LDH-5, hepatic)\nglyoxylate + NADH → OXALATE\n★ NEDOSIRAN / STIRIPENTOL TARGET", fillcolor="#c8e6c9", penwidth=2.0];
    GRHPR_ENZ [label="GRHPR\nglyoxylate + NADPH → GLYCOLATE\nhydroxypyruvate → D-glycerate\nTHE CYTOSOLIC SALVAGE (lost in PH2)", fillcolor="#a5d6a7", penwidth=2.0];
    OX_HEP    [label="HEPATIC OXALATE\nTERMINAL — no human enzyme degrades it", fillcolor="#ffcc80", penwidth=2.4];
    HPYR      [label="HYDROXYPYRUVATE", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    LGLYCERATE [label="L-GLYCERATE\nmade by LDH when GRHPR is absent\n→ L-GLYCERIC ACIDURIA = PH2 marker", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    GLYCOLATE_C [label="CYTOSOLIC GLYCOLATE\nbenign dead end, freely filtered", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    NADH_RATIO [label="cytosolic NADH/NAD+ redox state\n(ethanol, fructose, hypoxia shift it)", fillcolor="#eceff1"];
    GLYOX_TOX [label="glyoxylate protein carbonylation /\nGSH depletion — the theoretical liability\nof blocking the DOWNSTREAM step", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    OX_SRC_HEP [label="OX_SRC_HEP\nHEPATOCYTE-DERIVED OXALATE\n(reachable by GalNAc-siRNA)", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.2, color="#37474f"];
    OX_SRC_EXTRAHEP [label="OX_SRC_EXTRAHEP\nEXTRAHEPATIC OXALATE\n(kidney, other tissues — NOT reachable\nby a hepatocyte-restricted drug)\nTHE PH2 NON-RESPONSE LIVES HERE", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.2, color="#37474f"];

    GLYOX_C -> LDHA_LIV [color=black];
    LDHA_LIV -> OX_HEP [color=black, label="J_LDH (irreversible)"];
    GLYOX_C -> GRHPR_ENZ [color=black];
    GRHPR_ENZ -> GLYCOLATE_C [color=black, label="salvage"];
    HPYR -> GRHPR_ENZ [color=black];
    HPYR -> LGLYCERATE [color=black, label="LDH (PH2 only)"];
    NADH_RATIO -> LDHA_LIV [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    GLYOX_C -> GLYOX_TOX [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    OX_HEP -> OX_SRC_HEP [color=black];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 5 — MITOCHONDRION / HYDROXYPROLINE ROUTE (PH3)
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_mito {
    label=<<B>5. HEPATOCYTE MITOCHONDRION — the hydroxyproline route and PH3</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#f4fbf5"; color="#2e7d32"; fontsize=12;

    MITO      [label="MITOCHONDRION", fillcolor="#e3f2fd", shape=box3d];
    HYP_OX    [label="4-hydroxyproline oxidase / dehydrogenase", fillcolor="#e8f5e9"];
    HOG       [label="4-HYDROXY-2-OXOGLUTARATE (HOG)\naccumulates in PH3", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    HOGA1_ENZ [label="HOGA1 aldolase\nHOG → pyruvate + GLYOXYLATE\n(lost in PH3)", fillcolor="#a5d6a7"];
    GLYOX_M   [label="MITOCHONDRIAL GLYOXYLATE", fillcolor="#ffe082"];
    DHG       [label="2,4-DIHYDROXYGLUTARATE (DHG)\nHOG reduction product\n→ PH3 diagnostic metabolite", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    HOG_INHIB [label="HOG inhibits mitochondrial GRHPR\nand disturbs citrate metabolism\n→ WHY LOSING AN UPSTREAM ALDOLASE\nSTILL RAISES OXALATE", fillcolor="#eceff1"];
    HYP_TRANS [label="mitochondrial glyoxylate export\nto cytosol", fillcolor="#eceff1"];

    HYP_OX -> HOG [color=black];
    HOG -> HOGA1_ENZ [color=black];
    HOGA1_ENZ -> GLYOX_M [color=black];
    HOG -> DHG [color=black, label="PH3: accumulates"];
    HOG -> HOG_INHIB [color=black];
    GLYOX_M -> HYP_TRANS [color=black];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 6 — OXALATE SYSTEMIC DISTRIBUTION AND SOLUBILITY LIMIT
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_dist {
    label=<<B>6. OXALATE DISTRIBUTION — and the solubility limit that defines systemic oxalosis</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#fffdf5"; color="#ef6c00"; fontsize=12;

    OX_PL   [label="PLASMA OXALATE (Pox)\nnormal 1-6 umol/L\nESKD-PH1 60-120 umol/L", fillcolor="#ffcc80", penwidth=2.4];
    OX_ECF  [label="rapidly exchanging ECF oxalate\n(Vd ≈ 0.2-0.3 L/kg)", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    OX_FREE [label="free (ultrafilterable) oxalate\n— minimal protein binding", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    CA_PL   [label="plasma ionised calcium", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    SS_PLASMA [label="PLASMA CaOx SUPERSATURATION\nSS_plasma = [Ca2+]·[Ox2-] / Ksp\nsolubility limit reached at\nPox ≈ 30 umol/L", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.4, color="#37474f"];
    DEPO_ON [label="SYSTEMIC DEPOSITION SWITCH\ndeposition rate ∝ max(0, Pox − Pox_crit)\n★ THE THRESHOLD, GENERATED NOT ASSUMED", fillcolor="#ffe0b2", penwidth=2.4];
    TOT_BURDEN [label="TOTAL BODY OXALATE BURDEN\n(the integral of everything unexcreted)", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.0];
    NUCLEATE_SYS [label="heterogeneous nucleation on\ncollagen, elastin, basement membrane", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];

    OX_PL -> OX_ECF [dir=both, color=black];
    OX_PL -> OX_FREE [color=black];
    OX_FREE -> SS_PLASMA [color=black];
    CA_PL -> SS_PLASMA [color="#1565c0"];
    SS_PLASMA -> DEPO_ON [color="#1565c0", penwidth=1.8];
    DEPO_ON -> NUCLEATE_SYS [color=black];
    DEPO_ON -> TOT_BURDEN [color=black];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 7 — BONE: THE RESERVOIR THAT BUFFERS THEN BETRAYS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_bone {
    label=<<B>7. BONE — the largest reservoir; it buffers before ESKD and releases after transplant</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#f5faff"; color="#1565c0"; fontsize=12;

    OX_BONE [label="SKELETAL OXALATE\nthe dominant tissue reservoir;\ncan hold thousands of umol/kg", fillcolor="#bbdefb", penwidth=2.2];
    BONE_IN  [label="influx: CaOx co-precipitation\nwith hydroxyapatite at the\nmineralisation front", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    BONE_OUT [label="efflux: OSTEOCLASTIC RESORPTION\nreleases oxalate back to plasma\n→ WHY Uox STAYS HIGH FOR MONTHS\nAFTER A NORMAL LIVER IS INSTALLED", fillcolor="#e3f2fd", penwidth=2.0];
    OSTEOCLAST [label="osteoclast activity\n(PTH, RANKL, acidosis, steroids,\nimmobilisation, growth)", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    OX_OSTEOPATHY [label="OXALATE OSTEOPATHY\nCaOx rosettes in trabeculae,\nsclerotic/lucent bands, pathological\nfractures, bone pain", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    MARROW_OX [label="marrow oxalate granulomas\n→ EPO-RESISTANT ANAEMIA\nand pancytopenia", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    GROWTH_FAIL [label="growth failure / short stature\n(children)", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    BONE_TURN_DRV [label="bone turnover as a DRUG-INDEPENDENT\nDETERMINANT of post-transplant Uox\n(a reservoir, not a source)", fillcolor="#eceff1"];

    BONE_IN -> OX_BONE [color=black];
    OX_BONE -> BONE_OUT [color=black];
    OSTEOCLAST -> BONE_OUT [color="#1565c0", penwidth=1.6];
    OX_BONE -> OX_OSTEOPATHY [color=black];
    OX_OSTEOPATHY -> MARROW_OX [color=black];
    OX_OSTEOPATHY -> GROWTH_FAIL [color=black];
    BONE_OUT -> BONE_TURN_DRV [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 8 — SOFT-TISSUE OXALOSIS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_soft {
    label=<<B>8. SOFT-TISSUE OXALOSIS — the disease past the threshold is not a kidney disease</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#fff5f5"; color="#c62828"; fontsize=12;

    OX_SOFT   [label="soft-tissue oxalate burden", fillcolor="#ffcdd2", penwidth=2.0];
    RETINA_OX [label="RETINAL / MACULAR oxalate\ncrystalline retinopathy,\nsubretinal fibrosis → VISION LOSS", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    MYOCARD   [label="MYOCARDIAL oxalosis\nconduction block, arrhythmia,\nrestrictive cardiomyopathy, sudden death", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    VESSEL_OX [label="MEDIAL ARTERIAL oxalate\nlivedo reticularis, acral gangrene,\ncalciphylaxis-like ulcers", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    NERVE_OX  [label="PERIPHERAL NERVE / vasa nervorum\nsensorimotor and autonomic\nneuropathy, mononeuritis multiplex", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    THYROID_OX [label="THYROID oxalate deposition\n(usually clinically silent)", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    JOINT_OX  [label="synovial CaOx → oxalate arthropathy,\nchondrocalcinosis, tenosynovitis", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    SKIN_OX   [label="cutaneous deposits, nodules,\nnon-healing ulcers", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    TEETH_OX  [label="dental / periodontal deposits", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    IRREVERSIBLE [label="deposition is SLOWLY reversible at best\n— removal half-life measured in\nMONTHS-YEARS, hence the value of\ntreating BEFORE the threshold", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.0];

    OX_SOFT -> RETINA_OX [color=black];
    OX_SOFT -> MYOCARD [color=black];
    OX_SOFT -> VESSEL_OX [color=black];
    OX_SOFT -> NERVE_OX [color=black];
    OX_SOFT -> THYROID_OX [color=black];
    OX_SOFT -> JOINT_OX [color=black];
    OX_SOFT -> SKIN_OX [color=black];
    OX_SOFT -> TEETH_OX [color=black];
    OX_SOFT -> IRREVERSIBLE [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 9 — RENAL OXALATE HANDLING
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_renal {
    label=<<B>9. RENAL HANDLING — the only sink that matters, and the one being destroyed</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#f5faff"; color="#1565c0"; fontsize=12;

    GFR       [label="GFR / eGFR\n(mL/min/1.73 m²)", fillcolor="#90caf9", penwidth=2.2];
    NEPHRONS  [label="viable nephron number\n(fraction of normal)", fillcolor="#bbdefb", penwidth=2.0];
    SNGFR     [label="single-nephron hyperfiltration\ncompensates early loss → masks\nnephron attrition until late", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    FILT_OX   [label="filtered oxalate load\n= GFR × Pox_free", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    SEC_OX    [label="net tubular SECRETION of oxalate\n(SLC26A6-mediated)\nCl_ox / Cl_creatinine ≈ 1.0-1.5", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    REABS_OX  [label="limited passive reabsorption", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    CL_OX     [label="RENAL OXALATE CLEARANCE\nCl_ox = f_sec × GFR\nTHE DENOMINATOR OF THE DISEASE", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.4, color="#37474f"];
    TUB_OX_CONC [label="TUBULAR FLUID [oxalate]\nrises along the nephron as water\nis reabsorbed → peaks in the\nmedullary collecting duct", fillcolor="#fff8e1", penwidth=2.0];
    LDHA_KID  [label="RENAL LDHA\nlocal tubular glyoxylate → oxalate\n★ NOT silenced by a\nhepatocyte-restricted siRNA", fillcolor="#c8e6c9", penwidth=2.0];
    GLYOX_FILT [label="filtered glyoxylate + glycolate\ndelivered to the tubule", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    U_OX      [label="URINARY OXALATE EXCRETION (Uox)\nnormal <0.46 mmol/1.73m²/24h\nPH1 typically 1.0-2.5", fillcolor="#e0f7fa", penwidth=2.2];
    U_FLOW    [label="urine flow rate\n(the denominator of concentration)", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    MEDULLARY [label="medullary tonicity / countercurrent\nconcentrating mechanism\n= the crystallisation hot spot", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    OX_KID_TIS [label="RENAL PARENCHYMAL oxalate\n(nephrocalcinosis burden)", fillcolor="#ffcdd2", penwidth=2.0];

    NEPHRONS -> GFR [color="#1565c0", penwidth=2.0];
    NEPHRONS -> SNGFR [color="#1565c0"];
    SNGFR -> GFR [color="#1565c0", style=dashed, label="compensation"];
    GFR -> FILT_OX [color=black];
    GFR -> CL_OX [color=black, penwidth=1.8];
    SEC_OX -> CL_OX [color="#1565c0"];
    REABS_OX -> CL_OX [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    CL_OX -> U_OX [color=black, penwidth=2.0];
    FILT_OX -> TUB_OX_CONC [color=black];
    SEC_OX -> TUB_OX_CONC [color="#1565c0"];
    U_FLOW -> TUB_OX_CONC [style=dashed, color="#c62828", label="dilutes"];
    MEDULLARY -> TUB_OX_CONC [color="#1565c0"];
    GLYOX_FILT -> LDHA_KID [color=black];
    LDHA_KID -> TUB_OX_CONC [color=black, label="LOCAL synthesis"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 10 — CRYSTALLISATION PHYSICAL CHEMISTRY
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_cryst {
    label=<<B>10. CRYSTALLISATION — a RATIO, not a flux: the target of therapy that changes no mass balance</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#fffdf5"; color="#f9a825"; fontsize=12;

    U_CA   [label="urinary CALCIUM\n(hypercalciuria is common in PH3\nand modifies risk in PH1)", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    U_CIT  [label="urinary CITRATE\ncomplexes Ca2+ AND inhibits\ncrystal growth/aggregation", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    U_MG   [label="urinary MAGNESIUM\ncomplexes oxalate", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    U_PH   [label="urine pH\n(CaOx solubility is pH-insensitive —\nunlike uric acid and cystine)", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    U_VOL  [label="URINE VOLUME\nthe most powerful and cheapest\nlever on the ratio", fillcolor="#fff8e1", penwidth=2.0];
    OPN_UMOD [label="macromolecular inhibitors\nosteopontin, uromodulin, nephrocalcin,\nbikunin, Tamm-Horsfall protein", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    RSS    [label="RELATIVE SUPERSATURATION (RSS CaOx)\nRSS = AP(CaOx) / Ksp\nTHE STONE DRIVER", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.4, color="#37474f"];
    NUCLEATION [label="homogeneous + heterogeneous\nnucleation (RSS > ~8-10)", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    GROWTH [label="crystal growth", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    AGGREG [label="aggregation", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    COM_COD [label="COM (monohydrate, whewellite) vs\nCOD (dihydrate, weddellite)\nCOM adheres more avidly →\nPH urine favours COM", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    RETENTION [label="CRYSTAL RETENTION\n(the step that converts crystalluria\ninto disease)", fillcolor="#ffebee", penwidth=2.0];
    RANDALL [label="Randall plaque / plugs at the\npapillary tip", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    STONE  [label="STONE FORMATION\nradio-opaque CaOx calculi,\noften bilateral and recurrent", fillcolor="#f3e5f5", penwidth=2.0];
    NC     [label="NEPHROCALCINOSIS\nmedullary → cortical;\nthe PH-specific pattern", fillcolor="#f3e5f5", penwidth=2.0];
    CRYSTALLURIA [label="crystalluria (COM crystals on\nfresh urine microscopy)", fillcolor="#e0f7fa"];
    OBSTRUCT [label="ureteric obstruction, colic,\npost-obstructive AKI", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    UTI    [label="stone-associated UTI /\nurosepsis", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];

    U_CA -> RSS [color="#1565c0", penwidth=1.6];
    U_CIT -> RSS [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=1.6];
    U_MG -> RSS [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    U_VOL -> RSS [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=2.0];
    U_PH -> RSS [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    RSS -> NUCLEATION [color="#1565c0", penwidth=1.8];
    NUCLEATION -> GROWTH [color=black];
    GROWTH -> AGGREG [color=black];
    AGGREG -> RETENTION [color=black];
    OPN_UMOD -> AGGREG [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    OPN_UMOD -> RETENTION [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    COM_COD -> RETENTION [color="#1565c0"];
    RETENTION -> STONE [color=black, penwidth=1.6];
    RETENTION -> NC [color=black, penwidth=1.6];
    RETENTION -> RANDALL [color=black];
    NUCLEATION -> CRYSTALLURIA [color=black];
    STONE -> OBSTRUCT [color=black];
    STONE -> UTI [color=black];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 11 — CRYSTAL-INDUCED TUBULOINTERSTITIAL INJURY
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_injury {
    label=<<B>11. CRYSTAL-INDUCED INJURY — the mechanistic bridge from crystals to lost GFR</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#fff5f5"; color="#c62828"; fontsize=12;

    ADHESION [label="crystal-epithelial ADHESION\nCD44, hyaluronan, annexin-II,\nphosphatidylserine exposure", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    INTERNAL [label="crystal internalisation /\nintratubular plugging", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    TUB_INJ  [label="proximal tubular injury\nKIM-1, NGAL, L-FABP release", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    ROS      [label="mitochondrial ROS,\nlipid peroxidation", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    NLRP3    [label="NLRP3 INFLAMMASOME\ncrystal = classic DAMP;\nASC + caspase-1 assembly", fillcolor="#ffcdd2", penwidth=2.0];
    IL1B     [label="IL-1beta / IL-18\n(mature, caspase-1-cleaved)", fillcolor="#ffcdd2"];
    IL6_TNF  [label="IL-6, TNF-alpha, MCP-1/CCL2", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    MACROPH  [label="monocyte/macrophage influx;\nM1 polarisation; granuloma formation\naround crystals", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    MULTINUC [label="multinucleate giant cells\n(crystal granuloma)", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    TGFB     [label="TGF-beta1", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    EMT      [label="partial EMT / tubular\ndedifferentiation, G2/M arrest", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    FIBRO    [label="INTERSTITIAL FIBROSIS\nmyofibroblast expansion,\ncollagen I/III deposition", fillcolor="#ffcdd2", penwidth=2.0];
    ATUBULAR [label="atubular glomeruli /\nglomerulotubular disconnection", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    NEPHRON_LOSS [label="NEPHRON LOSS\n(irreversible)", fillcolor="#ef9a9a", penwidth=2.4];
    NECROINFL [label="regulated necrosis (necroptosis,\nferroptosis) of tubular cells", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    AKI_EPI  [label="acute crystalline nephropathy\n(acute-on-chronic GFR drops that\nratchet the disease downward)", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    ANTI_IL1 [label="anti-IL-1 / NLRP3 blockade\n— MECHANISTICALLY IMPLIED,\nNOT AN APPROVED THERAPY\n(a falsifiable prediction of this map)", fillcolor="#fce4ec", style="filled,rounded,dashed"];

    RETENTION -> ADHESION [color=black];
    ADHESION -> INTERNAL [color=black];
    INTERNAL -> TUB_INJ [color=black];
    TUB_INJ -> ROS [color="#1565c0"];
    INTERNAL -> NLRP3 [color="#1565c0", penwidth=1.8];
    ROS -> NLRP3 [color="#1565c0"];
    NLRP3 -> IL1B [color=black, penwidth=1.8];
    IL1B -> MACROPH [color="#1565c0", penwidth=1.6];
    IL1B -> IL6_TNF [color="#1565c0"];
    MACROPH -> MULTINUC [color=black];
    MACROPH -> TGFB [color="#1565c0", penwidth=1.6];
    IL6_TNF -> TGFB [color="#1565c0"];
    TGFB -> EMT [color="#1565c0"];
    TGFB -> FIBRO [color="#1565c0", penwidth=2.0];
    EMT -> FIBRO [color="#1565c0"];
    FIBRO -> ATUBULAR [color=black];
    ATUBULAR -> NEPHRON_LOSS [color=black, penwidth=2.0];
    TUB_INJ -> NECROINFL [color="#1565c0"];
    NECROINFL -> NEPHRON_LOSS [color=black];
    INTERNAL -> AKI_EPI [color=black];
    AKI_EPI -> NEPHRON_LOSS [color=black];
    ANTI_IL1 -> NLRP3 [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=1.8];
    ANTI_IL1 -> IL1B [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 12 — THE POSITIVE FEEDBACK LOOP
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_loop {
    label=<<B>12. THE RUNAWAY — a positive feedback loop whose gain RISES as GFR falls</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#f7f7f7"; color="#37474f"; fontsize=12; penwidth=2.4;

    L1 [label="① nephron loss", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=1.8];
    L2 [label="② GFR falls\n→ renal oxalate clearance falls", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=1.8];
    L3 [label="③ production now EXCEEDS clearance\n→ plasma oxalate rises ∝ 1/GFR", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=1.8];
    L4 [label="④ Pox crosses ~30 umol/L\n→ tissue + renal deposition begins", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=1.8];
    L5 [label="⑤ nephrocalcinosis + crystal\ninflammation destroy more nephrons", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=1.8];
    LOOP_GAIN [label="LOOP GAIN\nrises steeply below eGFR ≈ 30-45\n→ EXPLAINS THE ABRUPT TERMINAL\nDECLINE WITHOUT A NEW MECHANISM", fillcolor="#ffe0b2", penwidth=2.4];
    POINT_NR [label="POINT OF NO RETURN\nbeyond which stopping production\nno longer stops progression,\nbecause the bone reservoir\nkeeps feeding the plasma pool", fillcolor="#ffcdd2", penwidth=2.4];
    EARLY_TX [label="→ THE ARGUMENT FOR EARLY DIAGNOSIS\nis loop-gain arithmetic, not sentiment", fillcolor="#eceff1"];

    L1 -> L2 -> L3 -> L4 -> L5 -> L1 [color="#c62828", penwidth=2.2];
    L2 -> LOOP_GAIN [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    LOOP_GAIN -> POINT_NR [color="#c62828", penwidth=1.8];
    POINT_NR -> EARLY_TX [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 13 — GUT-KIDNEY OXALATE AXIS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_gut {
    label=<<B>13. GUT-KIDNEY AXIS — small in PH, decisive in enteric hyperoxaluria (same equation, different source)</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#fffdf5"; color="#f9a825"; fontsize=12;

    GUT_LUMEN [label="intestinal luminal oxalate", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
    ABS_PARA  [label="paracellular absorption\n(colon > ileum)", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    ABS_TRANS [label="transcellular absorption\n(SLC26A6, SLC26A3)", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    CA_BINDING [label="luminal Ca2+ binds oxalate\n→ unabsorbable CaOx\nWHY CALCIUM RESTRICTION IS WRONG", fillcolor="#eceff1"];
    ENT_SECR  [label="ENTERIC SECRETION of oxalate\n(plasma → lumen via SLC26A6)\nan alternative sink that RISES\nas plasma oxalate rises", fillcolor="#e3f2fd", penwidth=2.0];
    OXF       [label="OXALOBACTER FORMIGENES\nobligate oxalate-degrading anaerobe\noxalyl-CoA decarboxylase + formyl-CoA\ntransferase (oxc / frc)", fillcolor="#e8f5e9", penwidth=2.0];
    OXF_LOSS  [label="loss of colonisation after\nantibiotic exposure\n(a modifiable risk factor)", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    OTHER_DEG [label="Lactobacillus / Bifidobacterium /\nEnterococcus oxalate degradation\n(minor)", fillcolor="#e8f5e9"];
    FAT_MALABS [label="FAT MALABSORPTION\n(bariatric surgery, short bowel,\nIBD, cystic fibrosis, pancreatic\ninsufficiency)", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    FFA_CA    [label="free fatty acids sequester luminal Ca2+\n→ oxalate stays soluble\n+ bile acids raise mucosal permeability", fillcolor="#eceff1"];
    ENTERIC_HO [label="ENTERIC (SECONDARY) HYPEROXALURIA\nsame RSS and same CKD mechanism,\nbut the source is DIETARY, so enteric\ndegradation WORKS here and is\nnearly futile in PH1\n★ ONE EQUATION, TWO DISEASES", fillcolor="#ffe0b2", penwidth=2.4];

    DIET_OXALATE -> GUT_LUMEN [color=black];
    GUT_LUMEN -> ABS_PARA [color=black];
    GUT_LUMEN -> ABS_TRANS [color=black];
    CA_BINDING -> GUT_LUMEN [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=1.6];
    OXF -> GUT_LUMEN [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=1.8, label="degrades"];
    OTHER_DEG -> GUT_LUMEN [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    OXF_LOSS -> OXF [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    FAT_MALABS -> FFA_CA [color=black];
    FFA_CA -> ABS_PARA [color="#1565c0", penwidth=1.8];
    FFA_CA -> ENTERIC_HO [color="#1565c0", penwidth=1.8];
    OX_PL -> ENT_SECR [color=black];
    ENT_SECR -> GUT_LUMEN [color=black];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 14 — siRNA PK/PD (GalNAc / ASGPR / RISC)
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_sirna {
    label=<<B>14. GalNAc-siRNA PK/PD — a plasma half-life of hours driving a quarterly dose, and why delivery decides indication</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#fdf3f7"; color="#ad1457"; fontsize=12;

    LUM   [label="LUMASIRAN\nGalNAc-siRNA vs HAO1 (glycolate oxidase)\n3 mg/kg SC monthly ×3, then QUARTERLY\n(>20 kg)", fillcolor="#f8bbd0", penwidth=2.2];
    NED   [label="NEDOSIRAN\nGalNAc-siRNA vs LDHA\n160 mg SC MONTHLY (≥50 kg)", fillcolor="#f8bbd0", penwidth=2.2];
    SC_DEPOT [label="subcutaneous depot\nfirst-order absorption", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    PLASMA_SI [label="plasma siRNA\nt½ ≈ 4-6 h — SHORT", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    ASGPR [label="ASIALOGLYCOPROTEIN RECEPTOR (ASGPR)\n~5×10⁵ copies per HEPATOCYTE,\nrecycling t½ ~15 min,\nEXPRESSED ESSENTIALLY NOWHERE ELSE\n★ THE SOURCE OF TISSUE SELECTIVITY", fillcolor="#f8bbd0", penwidth=2.4];
    TRIVALENT [label="trivalent GalNAc ligand\n→ nanomolar avidity for ASGPR", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    ENDOSOME [label="clathrin endocytosis → endosome;\nslow, inefficient ENDOSOMAL ESCAPE\n(depot within the cell)", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    RISC  [label="RISC-LOADED siRNA (Ago2)\nintracellular t½ WEEKS-MONTHS\n★ THE PK/PD DISCONNECT THAT MAKES\nQUARTERLY DOSING RATIONAL", fillcolor="#f48fb1", penwidth=2.4];
    ESC_CHEM [label="ESC / ESC+ chemistry: 2'-OMe, 2'-F,\nphosphorothioate ends → nuclease\nstability, no innate immune activation", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    MRNA_CUT [label="Ago2-catalysed mRNA cleavage\n(catalytic, sub-stoichiometric)", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    HAO1_MRNA [label="HAO1 mRNA", fillcolor="#e8f5e9"];
    LDHA_MRNA [label="LDHA mRNA", fillcolor="#e8f5e9"];
    PROT_TURN [label="target PROTEIN turnover sets the LAG\nbetween mRNA knockdown and\nmetabolic effect (weeks)", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=1.8];
    GLYCOLATE_RISE [label="PLASMA / URINARY GLYCOLATE RISES\n— an ON-TARGET 'abnormal' laboratory\nvalue that is the RECEIPT for\nlumasiran target engagement", fillcolor="#e0f7fa", penwidth=2.2];
    HEP_ONLY [label="HEPATOCYTE-RESTRICTED knockdown\n→ CANNOT touch OX_SRC_EXTRAHEP\n→ PH1 responds, PH2 does not\n★ DELIVERY, NOT TARGET, DECIDES", fillcolor="#ffe0b2", penwidth=2.4];
    ISR_AE [label="injection-site reactions\n(the dominant adverse event)", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    LUM_LOAD [label="loading-then-maintenance schedule\nis a RISC-accumulation design,\nnot an empirical convention", fillcolor="#eceff1"];

    LUM -> SC_DEPOT [color=black]; NED -> SC_DEPOT [color=black];
    TRIVALENT -> ASGPR [color="#1565c0"];
    SC_DEPOT -> PLASMA_SI [color=black];
    PLASMA_SI -> ASGPR [color=black];
    ASGPR -> ENDOSOME [color=black];
    ENDOSOME -> RISC [color=black, penwidth=1.8];
    ESC_CHEM -> RISC [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    RISC -> MRNA_CUT [color=black, penwidth=1.8];
    MRNA_CUT -> HAO1_MRNA [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=1.8];
    MRNA_CUT -> LDHA_MRNA [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=1.8];
    HAO1_MRNA -> GO_HAO1 [color=black, label="translation"];
    LDHA_MRNA -> LDHA_LIV [color=black, label="translation"];
    PROT_TURN -> GO_HAO1 [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    ASGPR -> HEP_ONLY [style=dashed, color="#78909c", penwidth=1.8];
    HEP_ONLY -> OX_SRC_EXTRAHEP [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    GO_HAO1 -> GLYCOLATE_RISE [style=dashed, color="#0097a7", label="blocked → substrate\naccumulates"];
    LUM -> ISR_AE [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    RISC -> LUM_LOAD [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    LDHA_MRNA -> LDHA_KID [style=dashed, color="#78909c", label="NOT reached"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 15 — PYRIDOXINE / CHAPERONE RESCUE
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_b6 {
    label=<<B>15. PYRIDOXINE — the only genotype-gated therapy: a cofactor acting as a chaperone</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#fdf3f7"; color="#ad1457"; fontsize=12;

    PN     [label="PYRIDOXINE (vitamin B6)\n5-20 mg/kg/day PO", fillcolor="#f8bbd0", penwidth=2.0];
    PN_ABS [label="intestinal absorption → hepatic\npyridoxal kinase → PNP oxidase", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    PLP_PL [label="plasma PLP", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    CHAP_MECH [label="MECHANISM IS NOT SIMPLE COFACTOR\nREPLETION — PLP stabilises the folding\nintermediate and restores PEROXISOMAL\nIMPORT of G170R/F152I protein", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.0];
    B6_RESP [label="RESPONDERS: G170R and F152I\n(especially homozygous)\n→ ~30-50% Uox reduction", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    B6_NONRESP [label="NON-RESPONDERS: null alleles,\nPLP-binding-site mutants (G82E)\n→ ZERO effect at any dose\n★ A STRUCTURAL NULL, NOT A DOSE ISSUE", fillcolor="#ffebee", penwidth=2.0];
    B6_NEURO [label="dose-limiting sensory neuronopathy\nat high chronic doses\n(the reason for a ceiling)", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    B6_CEIL  [label="response saturates once AGT is\nfully PLP-loaded → dose escalation\nbeyond ~10 mg/kg/day buys little", fillcolor="#eceff1"];

    PN -> PN_ABS -> PLP_PL [color=black];
    PLP_PL -> PLP_LIV [color=black];
    PLP_LIV -> CHAP_MECH [color="#1565c0"];
    CHAP_MECH -> AGT_MISTGT [style=dashed, color="#c62828", label="restores\ntargeting"];
    CHAP_MECH -> B6_RESP [color="#1565c0"];
    ALL_G170R -> B6_RESP [color="#1565c0", style=dashed];
    ALL_F152I -> B6_RESP [color="#1565c0", style=dashed];
    ALL_NULL -> B6_NONRESP [color="#1565c0", style=dashed];
    ALL_G82E -> B6_NONRESP [color="#1565c0", style=dashed];
    PN -> B6_NEURO [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    PN -> B6_CEIL [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 16 — SMALL MOLECULES, GENE THERAPY, EXPERIMENTAL
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_exp {
    label=<<B>16. SMALL MOLECULES AND GENE THERAPY — the same targets reached by different routes</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#fdf3f7"; color="#ad1457"; fontsize=12;

    STP   [label="STIRIPENTOL\nrepurposed antiepileptic; LDH5 inhibitor\nORAL SMALL MOLECULE → reaches\nLIVER *AND* KIDNEY\n(evidence conflicting)", fillcolor="#f8bbd0", penwidth=2.0];
    STP_ADV [label="a small molecule can silence RENAL\nLDHA that an siRNA cannot —\nthe distribution argument run in reverse", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.0];
    GO_INHIB [label="small-molecule GO/HAO1 inhibitors\n(e.g. salicylate analogues,\nCCPST-class compounds) — preclinical", fillcolor="#fce4ec", style="filled,rounded,dashed"];
    AAV_AGXT [label="AAV8-AGXT liver gene addition\n(preclinical / early clinical)\nrestores the MISSING enzyme rather\nthan reducing substrate", fillcolor="#fce4ec", style="filled,rounded,dashed"];
    CRISPR_HAO1 [label="CRISPR/base-editing HAO1 knockout\n— a permanent, single-administration\nversion of lumasiran", fillcolor="#fce4ec", style="filled,rounded,dashed"];
    LNP_MRNA [label="LNP-mRNA AGT replacement", fillcolor="#fce4ec", style="filled,rounded,dashed"];
    OXDC_ENZ [label="oral/crystallised oxalate\ndecarboxylase (OxDC) enzyme therapy\n— degrades LUMINAL oxalate only", fillcolor="#fce4ec", style="filled,rounded,dashed"];
    CHAPERONE_SM [label="pharmacological chaperones\n(dequalinium-class) for AGT folding —\nB6-independent rescue", fillcolor="#fce4ec", style="filled,rounded,dashed"];
    COMBO_LOGIC [label="COMBINATION LOGIC\nLayer A (production) × Layer B (RSS)\nis multiplicative on stone risk;\nLayer A × Layer C is additive on balance", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.0];

    STP -> LDHA_LIV [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=1.8];
    STP -> LDHA_KID [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=1.8];
    STP -> STP_ADV [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    GO_INHIB -> GO_HAO1 [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    AAV_AGXT -> AGT_HOLO [color="#1565c0", penwidth=1.6];
    LNP_MRNA -> AGT_HOLO [color="#1565c0"];
    CRISPR_HAO1 -> HAO1_MRNA [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    CHAPERONE_SM -> AGT_APO [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    OXDC_ENZ -> GUT_LUMEN [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 17 — SUPPORTIVE / CRYSTALLISATION-DIRECTED THERAPY
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_supp {
    label=<<B>17. LAYER B THERAPY — changes no flux, halves the risk</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#fdf3f7"; color="#ad1457"; fontsize=12;

    HYPERHYD [label="HYPERHYDRATION\n2-3 L/m²/day, including OVERNIGHT\n(gastrostomy in infants)\nmass balance UNCHANGED, RSS halved", fillcolor="#f8bbd0", penwidth=2.2];
    KCIT    [label="POTASSIUM CITRATE\n0.10-0.15 g/kg/day\ncomplexes Ca2+, inhibits growth,\ncorrects the acidosis of CKD", fillcolor="#f8bbd0", penwidth=2.0];
    MG_SUPP [label="magnesium supplementation\n(complexes oxalate)", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    NEUT_PHOS [label="neutral orthophosphate\n(inhibitor; largely historical)", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    THIAZ   [label="thiazide (only if hypercalciuric)", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    DIET_ADV [label="dietary advice: avoid oxalate-rich foods\nand high-dose vitamin C;\nDO NOT restrict calcium;\nmoderate animal protein", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    AVOID_ASC [label="avoid ascorbate megadose\n(a removable source term)", fillcolor="#fce4ec"];
    LAYER_B_LIMIT [label="LAYER B PROTECTS THE KIDNEY BUT\nNEVER PREVENTS SYSTEMIC OXALOSIS —\nthe balance is still unclosed\n★ THE LIMIT OF SUPPORTIVE CARE", fillcolor="#ffe0b2", penwidth=2.4];

    HYPERHYD -> U_VOL [color="#1565c0", penwidth=2.2];
    KCIT -> U_CIT [color="#1565c0", penwidth=2.0];
    MG_SUPP -> U_MG [color="#1565c0"];
    NEUT_PHOS -> OPN_UMOD [color="#1565c0"];
    THIAZ -> U_CA [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    DIET_ADV -> DIET_OXALATE [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    AVOID_ASC -> ASCORBATE [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    HYPERHYD -> LAYER_B_LIMIT [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    KCIT -> LAYER_B_LIMIT [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 18 — DIALYSIS KINETICS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_dial {
    label=<<B>18. DIALYSIS — Layer C, and an arithmetic demonstration of its insufficiency</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#f5faff"; color="#1565c0"; fontsize=12;

    HD    [label="HAEMODIALYSIS\noxalate is small (90 Da) and\nfreely dialysable — high extraction", fillcolor="#bbdefb", penwidth=2.0];
    HDF   [label="haemodiafiltration / high-flux,\nhigh-blood-flow, large surface area", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    PD    [label="peritoneal dialysis\nLOWER oxalate clearance per day\nthan intensive HD", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    DAILY_HD [label="DAILY / nocturnal extended HD\n(6-7 sessions per week) —\nthe only regimen that approaches balance", fillcolor="#bbdefb", penwidth=2.0];
    REBOUND [label="POST-DIALYSIS REBOUND\nPox refills from tissue within hours;\ntime-averaged Pox ≫ post-HD Pox\n★ WHY A GOOD POST-DIALYSIS NUMBER\nIS A MISLEADING NUMBER", fillcolor="#ffe0b2", penwidth=2.2];
    DIAL_ARITH [label="THE ARITHMETIC\nproduction in severe PH1 ≈ 4-7 mmol/day\n≈ 30-50 mmol/week;\nconventional 3×4 h HD removes only\na fraction of that\n→ CUMULATIVE POSITIVE BALANCE\n★ DIALYSIS CANNOT BE THE ANSWER ALONE", fillcolor="#ffcdd2", penwidth=2.4];
    DIAL_PLUS_A [label="Layer A + Layer C:\ncutting production makes an\notherwise-insufficient dialysis\nprescription sufficient", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.0];

    HD -> HDF [color="#1565c0"]; HD -> DAILY_HD [color="#1565c0"];
    HD -> REBOUND [color=black];
    HD -> DIAL_ARITH [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    PD -> DIAL_ARITH [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    DIAL_ARITH -> DIAL_PLUS_A [color="#1565c0"];
    HD -> OX_PL [style=dashed, color="#c62828", label="removes"];
    OX_BONE -> REBOUND [color=black, label="refills"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 19 — TRANSPLANTATION
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_tx {
    label=<<B>19. TRANSPLANTATION — replace the factory, not just the drain</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#f5faff"; color="#1565c0"; fontsize=12;

    KTX_ALONE [label="ISOLATED KIDNEY TRANSPLANT\nhistorically FAILS in PH1: the liver keeps\nproducing, and the mobilising bone burden\nfloods the new graft", fillcolor="#ffcdd2", penwidth=2.0];
    CLKT   [label="COMBINED LIVER-KIDNEY TRANSPLANT\nreplaces the SOURCE — the definitive\nanatomical answer to a mass-balance problem", fillcolor="#bbdefb", penwidth=2.2];
    SEQ_LKT [label="sequential liver-then-kidney", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    PRE_LTX [label="pre-emptive isolated LIVER transplant\n(before ESKD) — trades a functioning\nkidney's future for a liver operation now", fillcolor="#e3f2fd"];
    GRAFT_OX [label="EARLY GRAFT OXALATE NEPHROPATHY\nintensive peri-operative HD + high urine\noutput are mandatory while the\ntissue burden unloads", fillcolor="#ffebee", penwidth=2.0];
    UNLOAD [label="post-transplant oxalate UNLOADING\nUox stays elevated for MONTHS-YEARS\nfrom the BONE reservoir, with a\nNORMAL liver in place\n★ A RESERVOIR EFFECT, NOT A RELAPSE", fillcolor="#ffe0b2", penwidth=2.4];
    RNAI_SHIFT [label="★ THE PARADIGM SHIFT THIS MAP PREDICTS\nif a drug closes the mass balance,\nISOLATED KIDNEY TRANSPLANT becomes\nrational and the liver can be spared", fillcolor="#c8e6c9", penwidth=2.4];
    IMMUNO [label="immunosuppression: CNI nephrotoxicity\nadds a second injury to a kidney\nalready handling a crystal load", fillcolor="#ffebee"];

    KTX_ALONE -> GRAFT_OX [color=black, penwidth=1.8];
    OX_BONE -> UNLOAD [color=black, penwidth=1.8];
    UNLOAD -> GRAFT_OX [color="#1565c0", penwidth=1.8];
    CLKT -> OX_SRC_HEP [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=1.8, label="removes the factory"];
    SEQ_LKT -> CLKT [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    PRE_LTX -> OX_SRC_HEP [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    LUM -> RNAI_SHIFT [color="#1565c0", style=dashed];
    RNAI_SHIFT -> KTX_ALONE [color="#1565c0", style=dashed, label="makes viable"];
    IMMUNO -> NEPHRON_LOSS [color="#1565c0", style=dashed];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 20 — CLINICAL ENDPOINTS
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_end {
    label=<<B>20. CLINICAL ENDPOINTS</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#faf5fc"; color="#6a1b9a"; fontsize=12;

    E_STONE  [label="symptomatic stone events / year", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    E_PROC   [label="ureteroscopy, SWL, PCNL burden\n(and SWL is relatively contraindicated\nin dense PH stones)", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    E_NC     [label="nephrocalcinosis grade on ultrasound", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    E_EGFR   [label="eGFR slope (mL/min/1.73m²/year)", fillcolor="#f3e5f5", penwidth=2.0];
    E_ESKD   [label="ESKD / dialysis initiation\n(~20-50% of PH1 by age 25)", fillcolor="#f3e5f5", penwidth=2.2];
    E_OXALOSIS [label="clinically apparent SYSTEMIC OXALOSIS", fillcolor="#f3e5f5", penwidth=2.0];
    E_GROWTH [label="growth velocity / final height", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    E_ANEMIA [label="EPO-resistant anaemia", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    E_QOL    [label="pain, treatment burden (overnight\nfluids, dialysis), quality of life", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    E_MORT   [label="mortality (cardiac oxalosis, sepsis)", fillcolor="#f3e5f5"];
    E_DELAY  [label="DIAGNOSTIC DELAY\nmedian years from first stone to\ndiagnosis; a modifiable determinant\nof every endpoint above", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.0];

    STONE -> E_STONE [color=black]; E_STONE -> E_PROC [color=black];
    NC -> E_NC [color=black];
    NEPHRON_LOSS -> E_EGFR [color=black, penwidth=2.0];
    E_EGFR -> E_ESKD [color=black, penwidth=2.0];
    OX_SOFT -> E_OXALOSIS [color=black, penwidth=1.8];
    GROWTH_FAIL -> E_GROWTH [color=black];
    MARROW_OX -> E_ANEMIA [color=black];
    MYOCARD -> E_MORT [color=black];
    E_DELAY -> E_ESKD [color="#1565c0", style=dashed];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CLUSTER 21 — THE MEASUREMENT LAYER
     ================================================================ */
  subgraph cluster_meas {
    label=<<B>21. THE MEASUREMENT LAYER — the biomarker that inverts, and the assays that lie</B>>;
    style="filled,rounded"; fillcolor="#f0fafc"; color="#00838f"; fontsize=12; penwidth=2.2;

    M_UOX [label="24-h Uox (mmol/1.73m²/day)\nVALID while eGFR is preserved\n= production, essentially", fillcolor="#b2ebf2", penwidth=2.0];
    M_UOXCR [label="Uox : creatinine ratio\n(the only option in infants;\nage-dependent reference range)", fillcolor="#e0f7fa"];
    M_POX [label="PLASMA OXALATE (Pox)\nthe ONLY valid biomarker once\neGFR < ~30-45", fillcolor="#b2ebf2", penwidth=2.0];
    M_INVERT [label="★ THE INVERSION\nUox = Cl_ox × Pox. As GFR falls, Uox\nFALLS while the disease ACCELERATES.\nThere is a GFR at which dUox/dt changes\nSIGN with production unchanged.\nA FALLING Uox IN ADVANCED PH IS NOT\nA THERAPEUTIC SUCCESS.", fillcolor="#ffe0b2", penwidth=2.6, color="#e65100"];
    M_TRIALS [label="WHY ONE DRUG NEEDED TWO ENDPOINTS\nILLUMINATE-A (eGFR ≥30): 24-h Uox\nILLUMINATE-C (advanced CKD/dialysis): Pox\n— not a regulatory quirk but the\nconsequence of the inversion above", fillcolor="#e0f7fa", penwidth=2.2];
    M_GLYCOLATE [label="plasma / urinary GLYCOLATE\nRISES on lumasiran (on-target),\nnormal or high at baseline in PH1", fillcolor="#e0f7fa"];
    M_LGLYC [label="urinary L-GLYCERATE → PH2", fillcolor="#e0f7fa"];
    M_DHG [label="urinary DHG / HOG → PH3", fillcolor="#e0f7fa"];
    M_ASSAY1 [label="ASSAY TRAP 1 — EX VIVO OXALOGENESIS\nascorbate in the specimen converts to\noxalate after collection; samples must be\nACIDIFIED and processed promptly or Uox\nis spuriously high", fillcolor="#ffebee", penwidth=2.0];
    M_ASSAY2 [label="ASSAY TRAP 2 — Pox needs immediate\nacidification and rapid separation;\nCaOx precipitates in the tube", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    M_ASSAY3 [label="ASSAY TRAP 3 — a single 24-h collection\nis noisy (day-to-day CV 20-30%);\ncompleteness must be verified by\ncreatinine excretion", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
    M_GENETIC [label="GENETIC TESTING is now first-line;\nliver biopsy AGT assay reserved for\nunresolved cases", fillcolor="#e0f7fa"];
    M_RSS_MEAS [label="RSS/AP(CaOx) computed from a full\nurine profile (EQUIL2/JESS) — a\nCALCULATED, not measured, biomarker", fillcolor="#e0f7fa"];
    M_SURROGATE [label="SURROGATE VALIDITY QUESTION\nno completed trial has yet shown that\nlowering Uox changes eGFR SLOPE —\nthe model treats this as a PREDICTION\nto be falsified, not a fact", fillcolor="#eceff1", penwidth=2.2];

    U_OX -> M_UOX [color=black];
    M_UOX -> M_UOXCR [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    OX_PL -> M_POX [color=black];
    GFR -> M_INVERT [style=dashed, color="#e65100", penwidth=2.0];
    M_UOX -> M_INVERT [style=dashed, color="#e65100", penwidth=2.0];
    M_INVERT -> M_TRIALS [color="#00838f", penwidth=2.0];
    GLYCOLATE_RISE -> M_GLYCOLATE [color=black];
    LGLYCERATE -> M_LGLYC [color=black];
    DHG -> M_DHG [color=black];
    ASCORBATE -> M_ASSAY1 [style=dashed, color="#c62828"];
    M_UOX -> M_ASSAY3 [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    M_POX -> M_ASSAY2 [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    RSS -> M_RSS_MEAS [color=black];
    M_UOX -> M_SURROGATE [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
    E_EGFR -> M_SURROGATE [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  }

  /* ================================================================
     CROSS-CLUSTER WIRING — the mass balance itself
     ================================================================ */

  /* genotype → residual activity → the enzymology */
  ALL_G170R -> RESID_AGT [color="#1565c0"];
  ALL_F152I -> RESID_AGT [color="#1565c0"];
  ALL_I244T -> RESID_AGT [color="#1565c0"];
  ALL_G82E  -> RESID_AGT [color="#1565c0"];
  ALL_NULL  -> RESID_AGT [color="#1565c0"];
  RESID_AGT -> AGT_HOLO [color="#1565c0", penwidth=2.2];
  RESID_AGT -> PHENO_INF   [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  RESID_AGT -> PHENO_CHILD [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  RESID_AGT -> PHENO_ADULT [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  RESID_AGT -> PENETR [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  AGXT -> AGT_HOLO [color="#1565c0"];
  AGXT -> AGT_MISTGT [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  GRHPR -> GRHPR_ENZ [color="#1565c0"];
  HOGA1 -> HOGA1_ENZ [color="#1565c0"];
  SLC26A1 -> SEC_OX [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  SLC26A1 -> ENT_SECR [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];

  /* substrate supply → peroxisome / mitochondrion */
  DIET_GLYCOLATE -> GLYCOLATE_P [color=black];
  GLYCOLATE_C -> GLYCOLATE_P [dir=both, color=black];
  DIET_GLYCINE -> DAO [color=black];
  HYPRO_FLUX -> HYP_OX [color=black];
  FRUCTOSE -> HPYR [color=black];
  ASCORBATE -> OX_HEP [color=black, label="non-enzymatic"];

  /* peroxisome → cytosol */
  PEROX_LEAK -> GLYOX_C [color=black, penwidth=2.0, label="ESCAPE\n(the pathogenic flux)"];
  HYP_TRANS -> GLYOX_C [color=black];
  AGT_MISTGT -> GLYOX_M [style=dashed, color="#78909c", label="wrong compartment"];

  /* the terminal metabolite enters the body */
  OX_SRC_HEP -> OX_PL [color=black, penwidth=2.4, label="PRODUCTION"];
  OX_SRC_EXTRAHEP -> OX_PL [color=black, penwidth=2.0];
  LDHA_KID -> OX_SRC_EXTRAHEP [color=black];
  GRHPR_ENZ -> OX_SRC_EXTRAHEP [style=dashed, color="#78909c", label="PH2: extrahepatic\nsource"];
  ABS_PARA -> OX_PL [color=black, label="absorption"];
  ABS_TRANS -> OX_PL [color=black];

  /* the three sinks */
  OX_PL -> FILT_OX [color=black, penwidth=2.0];
  OX_PL -> BONE_IN [color=black, penwidth=1.8];
  OX_PL -> OX_SOFT [color=black, penwidth=1.8];
  OX_PL -> OX_KID_TIS [color=black, penwidth=1.8];
  BONE_OUT -> OX_PL [color=black, penwidth=1.8];
  DEPO_ON -> OX_SOFT [color="#1565c0", penwidth=2.0];
  DEPO_ON -> BONE_IN [color="#1565c0"];
  DEPO_ON -> OX_KID_TIS [color="#1565c0", penwidth=2.0];

  /* urine formation and the ratio */
  U_OX -> RSS [color="#1565c0", penwidth=2.2];
  TUB_OX_CONC -> RSS [color="#1565c0", penwidth=2.0];
  U_VOL -> U_FLOW [color="#1565c0"];

  /* crystals destroy the sink — the loop closes */
  OX_KID_TIS -> NEPHRON_LOSS [color="#c62828", penwidth=2.0];
  NC -> NEPHRON_LOSS [color="#c62828", penwidth=2.0];
  OBSTRUCT -> NEPHRON_LOSS [color="#c62828"];
  NEPHRON_LOSS -> NEPHRONS [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=2.2, label="depletes"];
  GFR -> L2 [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  OX_PL -> L3 [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  NEPHRON_LOSS -> L1 [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];

  /* CKD consequences that feed back on the chemistry */
  GFR -> ACIDOSIS [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  ACIDOSIS [label="metabolic acidosis of CKD\n→ hypocitraturia + bone buffering\n(loses an inhibitor AND mobilises\nthe reservoir)", fillcolor="#ffebee"];
  ACIDOSIS -> U_CIT [style=dashed, color="#c62828", penwidth=1.6];
  ACIDOSIS -> OSTEOCLAST [color="#1565c0"];
  GFR -> CKD_SEQ [style=dashed, color="#78909c"];
  CKD_SEQ [label="usual CKD sequelae\n(anaemia, CKD-MBD, hypertension,\ncardiovascular risk) superimposed\non the oxalosis", fillcolor="#ffebee"];

  /* endpoints from the measurement layer */
  M_POX -> E_OXALOSIS [style=dashed, color="#78909c", label="predicts"];
  M_INVERT -> E_EGFR [style=dashed, color="#e65100"];

  /* ---------- THE BALANCE SHEET, stated as a node ---------------- */
  BALANCE [label=<<B>THE MASS BALANCE — the model's single organising identity</B><BR/>
d(TOTAL BODY OXALATE)/dt = PRODUCTION − RENAL EXCRETION − ENTERIC ELIMINATION − DIALYTIC REMOVAL<BR/>
<BR/>
PRODUCTION is set by genotype and reduced only by LAYER A<BR/>
RENAL EXCRETION = Cl_ox × Pox, and Cl_ox is itself destroyed by the oxalate<BR/>
ENTERIC ELIMINATION is small in PH and decisive in enteric hyperoxaluria<BR/>
DIALYTIC REMOVAL is, by arithmetic, insufficient alone<BR/>
<BR/>
<I>Everything else on this map — stones, nephrocalcinosis, ESKD, retinopathy, cardiomyopathy,<BR/>
bone disease, anaemia, the biomarker inversion, graft loss — is where the residual went.</I>>,
           shape=note, fillcolor="#fffde7", color="#f57f17", penwidth=2.6, fontsize=11];

  TOT_BURDEN -> BALANCE [style=dashed, color="#f57f17", penwidth=2.0];
  CL_OX -> BALANCE [style=dashed, color="#f57f17", penwidth=2.0];
  DIAL_ARITH -> BALANCE [style=dashed, color="#f57f17"];
  ENT_SECR -> BALANCE [style=dashed, color="#f57f17"];
  OX_SRC_HEP -> BALANCE [style=dashed, color="#f57f17", penwidth=2.0];

  /* plasma glycolate — the lumasiran target-engagement marker */
  GLYCOLATE_PL_X [label="plasma GLYCOLATE\n(freely filtered, benign;\nrises on lumasiran)", fillcolor="#fff8e1"];
  GLYCOLATE_PL_X -> M_GLYCOLATE [color=black];
  GLYCOLATE_C -> GLYCOLATE_PL_X [color=black];
  GFR -> GLYCOLATE_PL_X [style=dashed, color="#78909c", label="cleared by"];
}
